{
  "_comment": [
    "Real run history of `CI` (workflow id 291989718, .github/workflows/ci.yml) for the two",
    "consecutive master runs behind #2030, captured from",
    "GET /repos/peterrichards-lr/lfr-tunnel/actions/runs/{id} and .../{id}/jobs on 2026-09-18.",
    "Newest first, trimmed to the fields the detector reads. Job and step names, conclusions",
    "and ordering are verbatim.",
    "",
    "  35251731344  c2f702e9  #2022 merged      conclusion: failure",
    "               `Test Suite (windows-latest)` -> failure, step `Run Tests` -> failure",
    "  35259669027  05d58a51  #2025, docs only  conclusion: success",
    "               `Test Suite (windows-latest)` -> SUCCESS, step `Run Tests` -> skipped",
    "",
    "The second run is why the run-level view is not enough. ci.yml deliberately generates every",
    "matrix leg on every run (#1365: three required contexts are named by OS, so a leg that is",
    "never generated blocks the merge forever), and takes the saving on the INSIDE via RUN_SUITE.",
    "So the Windows leg does not go missing and does not report `skipped` -- it reports `success`",
    "with `Checkout Code`, `Set up Go` and `Run Tests` all skipped. Comparing job conclusions",
    "alone reads that as recovery. Only the step conclusions show master was still red.",
    "",
    "Kept as a real fixture rather than a hand-written one for the same reason as",
    "docs-workflow-runs.json: the logic is proved against the failure it exists to catch."
  ],
